# 0002. Crawlers as Parser implementations in a registry

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-19

Each store is a package implementing one small `Parser` interface, and a registry lists them, so
adding a store doesn't touch the runner.

## Technical details
- **Interface** (`crawlers/common/interfaces.go`): `Name() string`,
  `Parse(keyword string) ([]Result, error)`; `Result` holds the product title and its
  `Variant`s (price, stock, properties map).
- **Registry** (`crawlers/registry/registry.go`): `All()` returns the parsers.
- **Runner** (`crawlers/main.go`): starts each parser for the keyword `laptop` in a goroutine
  and logs how many results it found; `wg.Wait()` after the loop, so they run in parallel
  (until 2026-11-19 it sat inside the loop and they ran one after another).
- **Amazon** (`crawlers/amazon/crawler.go`): colly v2 with a search collector feeding a product
  collector; visits `https://www.amazon.com/s?k=<keyword>`.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: Go 1.23, gocolly/colly v2 (goquery, htmlquery).
- Alternatives: one crawler per binary (more deploy units); a headless browser (handles JS
  pages, much heavier); official product APIs (where available, more reliable than scraping).
